        ],
        [
          "bakış",
          "look, gaze"
        ],
        [
          "zaman",
          "time"
        ]
      ],
      "quiz": [
        {
          "q": "Which form means « I like swimming »?",
          "options": [
            "Yüzmek seviyorum",
            "Yüzmeyi seviyorum",
            "Yüzme seviyorum"
          ],
          "a": 1,
          "why": "With sevmek, the action noun -ma takes the accusative: yüzme + yi = yüzmeyi."
        },
        {
          "q": "Which suffix gives « the way of walking »?",
          "options": [
            "-mak",
            "-ma",
            "-ış"
          ],
          "a": 2,
          "why": "-ış / -iş forms nouns of manner: yürüyüş, bakış, gülüş."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "va2-6",
      "level": "A2",
      "num": 6,
      "title": "Relative clauses: -an / -en and -dik",
      "tr": "Sıfat-fiiller",
      "goal": "Say « the student who works » or « the book I read » without a heavy relative clause.",
      "watch": "sıfat fiil -an -dik",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Turkish places the relative clause before the noun, like an adjective. <b>-an / -en</b> means « who does »: <tur>çalışan öğrenci</tur> (the student who works), <tur>gelen otobüs</tur> (the bus that is coming)."
        },
        {
          "t": "table",
          "caption": "Two families of relative clauses",
          "head": [
            "Suffix",
            "Meaning",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "<tur>-an / -en</tur>",
              "who does the action",
              "<tur>Türkçe konuşan arkadaş</tur> (the friend who speaks Turkish)"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>-dik / -dık</tur>",
              "that one does, that is done",
              "<tur>okuduğum kitap</tur> (the book I read)"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>-acak / -ecek</tur>",
              "that will do / that will be done",
              "<tur>gideceğim yer</tur> (the place I will go)"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "With <b>-dik</b>, you always need a possessive suffix showing who does the action: <tur>okuduğum kitap</tur> (the book I read), <tur>okuduğun kitap</tur> (the book you read), <tur>okuduğu kitap</tur> (the book he read), <tur>okuduğumuz kitap</tur> (the book we read)."
        },
