    {
      "id": "va2-7",
      "level": "A2",
      "num": 7,
      "title": "Intensified adjectives",
      "tr": "Pekiştirilmiş sıfatlar",
      "goal": "Say « very blue », « pure white », « completely black » with intensified adjectives.",
      "watch": "pekiştirilmiş sıfatlar",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "To intensify an adjective, Turkish often adds a syllable at the beginning, made of the first syllable + <b>m, p, r or s</b>: <tur>mavi → masmavi</tur> (pure blue), <tur>beyaz → bembeyaz</tur> (pure white), <tur>siyah → simsiyah</tur> (completely black)."
        },
        {
          "t": "table",
          "caption": "The most common intensifications",
          "head": [
            "Adjective",
            "Intensified form",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "<tur>mavi</tur>",
              "<tur>masmavi</tur>",
              "pure blue"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>beyaz</tur>",
              "<tur>bembeyaz</tur>",
              "pure white"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>siyah</tur>",
              "<tur>simsiyah</tur>",
              "completely black"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>yeşil</tur>",
              "<tur>yemyeşil</tur>",
              "pure green"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>kırmızı</tur>",
              "<tur>kıpkırmızı</tur>",
              "bright red"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>sarı</tur>",
              "<tur>sapsarı</tur>",
              "bright yellow"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>temiz</tur>",
              "<tur>tertemiz</tur>",
              "spotless"
            ],
            [
              "<tur>pembe</tur>",
              "<tur>pespembe</tur>",
              "pure pink"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "note",
          "kind": "tip",
          "tag": "A flexible rule",
          "text": "Not every adjective can be intensified this way. When no set form comes to mind, <tur>çok</tur> + adjective is always correct: <tur>çok güzel</tur>, <tur>çok yeni</tur>. Learn the most frequent intensified forms as expressions."
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "You can also intensify with <tur>çok</tur> (very), <tur>pek</tur> (quite, very), <tur>son derece</tur> (extremely) or <tur>fevkalade</tur> (remarkably). <tur>Çok</tur> is the universal solution when the prefixed form does not exist."
        },
        {
          "t": "ex",
          "items": [
            {
              "tr": "Deniz bugün masmavi.",
              "fr": "The sea is deep blue today."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Bembeyaz bir gömlek giydi.",
              "fr": "He put on a snow-white shirt."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Simsiyah bir kedi gördüm.",
              "fr": "I saw a pitch-black cat."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Oda tertemiz.",
              "fr": "The room is spotless."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "note",
          "kind": "info",
          "tag": "Colours and emotions",
          "text": "These forms are also used figuratively: <tur>kıpkırmızı</tur> can describe a face that has gone red, <tur>yemyeşil</tur> a lush landscape. The intensification adds an image, not just intensity."
        }
      ],
      "vocab": [
        [
          "mavi",
          "blue"
        ],
        [
          "beyaz",
          "white"
        ],
        [
          "siyah",
          "black"
        ],
        [
          "yeşil",
          "green"
        ],
        [
          "kırmızı",
          "red"
        ],
        [
          "sarı",
          "yellow"
        ],
        [
          "temiz",
          "clean"
        ],
        [
          "pembe",
          "pink"
        ],
        [
          "çok",
          "very"
        ],
        [
          "renk",
          "colour"
        ]
      ],
      "quiz": [
        {
          "q": "How do you intensify « mavi »?",
          "options": [
            "mavimavi",
            "masmavi",
            "mavimsi"
          ],
          "a": 1,
          "why": "The first syllable ma + m gives masmavi: pure blue."
        },
        {
          "q": "What does « tertemiz » mean?",
          "options": [
            "very dirty",
